# MCP Server Setup

Runbook for configuring `~/.factory/mcp.json` on a new machine.

## How `mcp.json` works

- Location: `~/.factory/mcp.json` (user-level config; available in every project).
- **Factory owns this file.** It is written to by `droid mcp add`, the `/mcp`
  manager (enable/disable toggles, registry adds), and persistent tool
  approvals. Droid auto-reloads it on change.
- It is **deliberately not managed by chezmoi.** Managing it would fight
  Factory's own writes (every toggle/add would be reverted on
  `chezmoi apply`) and approvals are per-machine anyway (see below).
- Config schema and behavior: <https://docs.factory.ai/harness/mcp>

## To set up a new machine

Paste the `mcpServers` entries you want below into `~/.factory/mcp.json`
(merge under the existing `"mcpServers": { ... }` object). Paths must be
absolute — Droid does **not** expand `$HOME` in `command`/`args`, only in
`env`/`headers`/`oauth` fields — so the snippets below use your real home
directory, already filled in.

> `connectTimeout` (and `timeout`) are **not settable via `droid mcp add`**,
> which is why this runbook uses paste-ready JSON instead of CLI commands.
> Use `droid mcp add` only for servers with no special options.

### All machines — gopls (Go language server)

Prerequisite: `gopls` built with MCP support at `~/go/bin/gopls`
(`go install golang.org/x/tools/gopls@latest`). See `gopls-mcp.md` for usage.

```json
"gopls": {
  "command": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/go/bin/gopls",
  "args": ["mcp"],
  "env": {
    "PATH": "/opt/homebrew/bin:{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/go/bin",
    "GOPATH": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/go",
    "GOCACHE": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Library/Caches/go-build",
    "GOMODCACHE": "{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/go/pkg/mod"
  },
  "connectTimeout": 60000,
  "disabled": false
}
```

Linux note: drop `/opt/homebrew/bin:` from `PATH` (or point it at
`/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin` if you use Linuxbrew), and set `GOCACHE` to
`{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.cache/go-build` instead of the macOS
`Library/Caches` path.

### Work machines only — atlassian, chronosphere, chronosphere-docs

```json
"atlassian": {
  "type": "http",
  "url": "https://mcp.atlassian.com/v1/mcp",
  "disabled": false
},
"chronosphere": {
  "type": "http",
  "url": "https://datarobot.chronosphere.io/api/mcp/mcp",
  "disabled": false
},
"chronosphere-docs": {
  "type": "http",
  "url": "https://docs.chronosphere.io/mcp",
  "disabled": false
}
```

### Optional — agentmemory

Only on machines that have the local `agentmemory` project checked out at
`~/workspace/agentmemory` (build it first: the `dist/cli.mjs` entrypoint must
exist).

```json
"agentmemory": {
  "command": "node",
  "args": ["{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/workspace/agentmemory/dist/cli.mjs", "mcp"],
  "env": {
    "AGENTMEMORY_URL": "http://localhost:3111"
  }
}
```

## After pasting

1. **Authenticate OAuth servers.** `atlassian` (and any other remote server
   requiring OAuth) shows "needs authentication" until you complete the
   browser flow: run `droid`, type `/mcp`, and authenticate. OAuth tokens are
   stored in your system keyring, not in `mcp.json`.
2. **Re-approve persistent permissions.** Approvals are bound to a stable
   fingerprint of each server's transport config (command+args, or URL) and
   are **per-machine** — they do not transfer between machines or from a
   previous setup. Approve tools on first use, or manage them with
   `droid mcp permissions list | revoke | clear`.
3. **Verify:** `droid mcp list` should report each server as `connected`
   (or `needs authentication` until you finish step 1).
